From 18ba703107f5ca3c73c87deb0d3d063b384a3369 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sungsu Ahn <sungsu_ahn@korea.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:51:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 48/51] Build-time node count (MEGALON_NODES, default 2) for
 N-VM runs

LOGICAL_NODE_NUM becomes a build parameter instead of a constant:
- C++: constants.h keeps 2 as the default; CMake MEGALON_NODES (2..15) adds
  -DLOGICAL_NODE_NUM=N only for N != 2, so a 2-node build compiles as before.
- Rust: build.rs reads env MEGALON_NODES (default 2) and passes it to
  constants.rs (const-parsed); rerun-if lines list every build input.
- cxl_port.h: kMaxNodes = LOGICAL_NODE_NUM (control block node_alive/phase).
- Mismatch guards: nr lib .features "nodes=N" checked by CMake (missing = 2),
  nr_logical_node_num() checked in PortContext::Init.
- Port tests: idle replaying extra nodes 2..N-1 in the two tests that wrap
  the log; the 128 B log entry size assertion applies to N = 2 only (GCDEntry
  holds N + 1 CNStatus, so the entry grows to 192 B at N = 4, 256 B at N = 8).
- object-test refuses a build with N != 2 (two-node test).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
